     Question
   As per recent requirements shared by the Nautilus application development team, they need custom images created for one of their projects. Several of the initial testing requirements are already been shared with DevOps team. Therefore, create a docker file /opt/docker/Dockerfile (please keep D capital of Dockerfile) on App server 2 in Stratos DC and configure to build an image with the following requirements:
a. 	Use ubuntu:24.04 as the base image.
b. 	Install apache2 and configure it to work on 5002 port. (do not update any other Apache configuration settings like document root etc).

   Solution

 a. Login into App server 2
     ssh steve@stapp02
    -Create the directory
     sudo mkdir -p /opt/docker
     cd /opt/docker
    -sudo vi Dockerfile
       Paste the following content
FROM ubuntu:24.04

RUN apt-get update && \
    apt-get install -y apache2 && \
    apt-get clean

RUN sed -i 's/Listen 80/Listen 5002/' /etc/apache2/ports.conf && \
    sed -i 's/:80/:5002/' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf

EXPOSE 5002

CMD ["/usr/sbin/apache2ctl", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]
    save and exit
 
 b. verify the file
      ls -l /opt/docker/Dockerfile
      cat /opt/docker/Dockerfile
  - Build the image
      docker build -t nautlius-apache:5002 /opt/docker
  - Run and test
      docker run -d --name apache5002 -p 5002:5002 nautlius-apache:5002
      curl http://localhost:5002

